#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055579} :activity/id #uuid "4dd99c93-ce32-53a9-b191-e8bddb7f8f7f" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048778 :topic/id #uuid "bdf6a63d-1183-5d54-9223-faab1de59819" :topic/math-academy-id 60} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055579 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186056005 :tutorial/content "A **compound statement** is a sentence that consists of two or more statements separated by logical connectors, such as the word \"and\" or the word \"or.\"\n\nFor example, the following sentence is a compound statement:\n\n$P: 2$ is an integer **and** $2$ is positive \n\nThe first statement is \"$2$ is an integer,\" and the second is \"$2$ is positive.\" These two statements are separated by the logical connector \"and.\"\n\nThe following sentence is also a compound statement:\n\n$7$ is odd **or** $7$ is even \n\nIn this case, the first statement is \"$7$ is odd,\" and the second statement is \"$7$ is even.\" These two statements are separated by the logical connector \"or.\" \n\nWe can express the logical connectives \"and\" and \"or\" using symbols:\n\n- The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\land$\". Notice that it resembles \"A\" for \"And.\"\n\n- The word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor$\".\n\nLet's translate the following sentence into symbolic form:\n\n$2$ is an integer **and** $2$ is positive \n\nTo start, we introduce the letters $A$ and $B$ to denote each individual statement:\n\n- $A:$ $2$ is an integer\n\n- $B:$  $2$ is positive\n\nThen, our sentence becomes\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{2 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is an integer} }_A \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textrm{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \\underbrace{2 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is positive} }_B,\n$$\n\nthat is, $A \\land B.$\n\nFinally, note the following terminology:\n\n- The statement \"$P$ and $Q$\" is called the **conjunction** of the statements $P$ and $Q.$\n\n- The statement \"$P$ or $Q$\" is called the **disjunction** of the statements $P$ and $Q.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "4570766f-a355-5a80-9756-cd94d76fed9c" :tutorial/math-academy-id 7962 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "4a197e18-2f93-5927-89e7-71b02eeb66ff" :step/math-academy-id 153494 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055580}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055580 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054641 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054365 :question/id #uuid "a8c9f90f-3c97-5a01-99b5-9a9f8b3eef66" :question/math-academy-id "e-12677"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93bc0caa-2352-5d02-9ccf-7267dff4be2c" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049002}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055055} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055507} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379025} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379040} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379055} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389663} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389768} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496234} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496281} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496313}] :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Compound Statements in Symbolic Form"} :step/id #uuid "9a7b96e3-5988-5977-a20a-8a97b636978b" :step/math-academy-id 153495 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055581}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055581 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054642 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054366 :question/id #uuid "e5a60113-14a0-5468-93b1-7f0eaa6e9a90" :question/math-academy-id "e-12678"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e2ea816-3a62-5167-9f08-17ebcf97c22e" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055037} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055038} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379070} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379077} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389841} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389848} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496223} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496236} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496270} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496272} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496275} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565446}] :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Nested Compound Statements in Symbolic Form"} :step/id #uuid "c089550c-a72d-5a29-a351-4052cea239c4" :step/math-academy-id 153498 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055582}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055582 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186056029 :tutorial/content "Let's now consider the truth values of the logical connector \"and\". We have the following key idea:\n\n*The statement $A \\land B$ is true if $A$ is true **and** $B$ is true. Otherwise, it is false.* \n\nLet's determine the truth values of the following compound statement:\n\n$2$ is positive **and** $2$ is even.\n\nWriting this in symbols, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{2\\text{ is positive}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{2\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nor, simply\n\n$$\nA\\land B.\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is true and $B$ is true, this compound statement is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∧B≡\\text{true}∧\\text{true}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this context, the symbol \"$\\equiv$\" means \"is logically equivalent to.\" \n\nLet's now consider a similar compound statement but with the $2$ replaced with a $3$ in the second statement.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{2\\text{ is positive}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{3\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can write this symbolically as follows:\n\n$$\nA\\land C\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is true and $C$ is false, this compound statement is false:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∧C≡\\text{true}∧\\text{false}≡\\text{false}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "e16d77df-210e-5934-90ce-44b096916261" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8142 :tutorial/title "Truth Values of Statements Containing the \"And\" Connective"} :step/id #uuid "237b49c1-2062-5a12-862e-cc6120dfe275" :step/math-academy-id 153501 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055583}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055583 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186056072 :tutorial/content "Let's now consider the truth values of the logical connector \"or\". We have the following key idea:\n\n*The statement $A \\lor B$ is true if $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or both $A$ and $B$ are true. Otherwise, it is false.* \n\nLet's consider some examples:\n\n- First, consider the following statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{2\\text{ is positive}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{2\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is true and $B$ is true, this compound statement is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∨B≡\\text{true}∨\\text{true}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, consider the following statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{2\\text{ is positive}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{3\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is true, this compound statement is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∨C≡\\text{true}∨\\text{false}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Now, consider the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{-2\\text{ is positive}}_{⏟}}_{D}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{2\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $B$ is true, this compound statement is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D∨B≡\\text{false}∨\\text{true}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, consider the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{-2\\text{ is positive}}_{⏟}}_{D}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{3\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $D$ and $C$ are both false, this compound statement is false:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D∨C≡\\text{false}∨\\text{false}≡\\text{false}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "3b0d24cd-f605-59b2-9f16-f053e9b74e8a" :tutorial/math-academy-id 9044 :tutorial/title "Truth Values of Statements Containing the \"Or\" Connective"} :step/id #uuid "1023b546-9b0c-52d3-9454-3a5adbb094ec" :step/math-academy-id 153502 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055584}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055584 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054643 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054368 :question/id #uuid "6497cb54-2453-5dd7-8b97-09e06280d774" :question/math-academy-id "e-12693"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "49ab93ca-16ca-5e57-835f-036b59f25d63" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055060} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055087} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378995} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379005} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379015} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389724} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389734} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496309} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496323}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Values of Compound Statements"} :step/id #uuid "96ad2c2e-7a64-57d5-9f83-02022e8509c3" :step/math-academy-id 153503 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055585}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055585 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054644 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054389 :question/id #uuid "9209c4e5-30e0-5933-9c41-32750b5301ad" :question/math-academy-id "e-12895"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c15e521-f848-5d9c-ba06-00550277b8cb" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055061} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055088} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379084} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379094} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389744} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389825} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496262} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496303} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496324} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565456}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Values of Complex Statements"} :step/id #uuid "3cd4f3c8-8abb-53a5-a3a4-5df352b82883" :step/math-academy-id 153506}] :activity/title "The \"And\" and \"Or\" Connectives" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186054914}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046668} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565517} :activity/id #uuid "71a8b3cb-fa15-5adb-be3d-13c0443f9e35" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048778 :topic/id #uuid "bdf6a63d-1183-5d54-9223-faab1de59819" :topic/math-academy-id 60} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565487 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565446 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12e69b24-bdab-519d-9db4-fa9f763bec4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "P∧(Q∨R)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564969} {:answer/id #uuid "40a41c4a-74f2-5a0d-80b4-6255b626fcc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(P∧Q)∨R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565033} {:answer/id #uuid "577b7d65-cc3e-5730-82a1-86c384479356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "P∨(Q∧R)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565072} {:answer/id #uuid "b1ad3c78-1256-5dff-9d91-4d2324618c7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(P∨Q)∧R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565203} {:answer/id #uuid "f27b8716-005f-5b70-a4d1-fcf5671b7cd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "P∧(Q∧R)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565305}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565072} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2accb16-6316-5d25-b406-7af92337b373" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9036632e-a4e5-591e-b6d4-bd5830e984df" :question/math-academy-id "q-177452" :question/problem "$\\sqrt{5}$ is rational, **or** $3|12$ **and** $3|18.$\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $P:\\sqrt{5}\\text{ is rational}$\n\n- $Q:3|12$\n\n- $R:3|18\\text{ }$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $\\sqrt{5}$ is rational. This corresponds to $P.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $3|12$ and $3|18.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{3|12}_{⏟}}_{Q}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{3|18}_{⏟}}_{R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $Q∧R.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{\\sqrt{5}\\text{ is rational}}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{3|12\\text{ and }3|18}_{⏟}}_{Q\\,∧\\,R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∨(Q∧R).$"} :step/id #uuid "0273e10d-6704-5bf2-969f-e05c1abc5298" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565516}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565516 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565456 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4290994a-4111-5f59-8d28-488485afe845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565035} {:answer/id #uuid "56b8008e-3e0e-50d5-b98d-6f1ae9548a59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565069}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565035} :answer-field/id #uuid "1de9cdf1-94b6-56c2-bf7d-3647210da7b1" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565335} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c62bc40-0349-5024-a000-9e42299ef3ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564958} {:answer/id #uuid "addf42f9-b92a-50aa-840e-9cebd676a066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565197}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564958} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d6f16fd-3b2c-5aaa-8d4b-bff5822eb1f4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565366} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cde20091-5ea0-5e89-8e56-3c6da49f96e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565246} {:answer/id #uuid "f6d52984-4570-5e61-afbd-0073a1b7199b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565311}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565311} :answer-field/id #uuid "c48b5f22-688c-554b-b977-496452316b1e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565382}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b08d6228-4d71-56ec-903b-067eaa383489" :question/math-academy-id "q-178163" :question/problem "$$\n{{0\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{\\{1,2\\}\\cap \\{1\\}=\\{1,2\\}}}\\,\\overset{∨}{\\overset{⏞}{\\text{or}}}\\,\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{2}{3}\\text{ is irrational}}}}_{⏟}}_{Q\\,∨\\,R}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $P$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $Q∨R$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $P∨(Q∨R)$ is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $P$ is true, $Q$ is false, and $R$ is false. Therefore, $Q∨R$ is false, but the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P∨(Q∨R) & ≡\\text{true}∨\\overset{\\text{false}}{\\overset{⏞}{(\\text{false}∨\\text{false})}} \\\\  & ≡\\text{true}∨\\text{false} \\\\  & ≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "7e1dd0ca-0641-5269-abe6-68b013d844af" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565538}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565517 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055037 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc55069c-667c-5e08-b2b0-341a1b91bc8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "R∨(S∨T)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051753} {:answer/id #uuid "d4920408-8a32-5926-8964-f320c3ee7ae1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "R∨(S∧T)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051754} {:answer/id #uuid "d8af7fc3-5f6b-5139-9b22-d82aba7b2766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(R∨S)∨T" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051755} {:answer/id #uuid "e1eff23a-ece4-5063-9fd2-b91ca4789a60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "R∧(S∧T)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051756} {:answer/id #uuid "e6d624ca-e16c-5795-906f-04ab06d6cdab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(R∧S)∨T" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051757}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051754} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4759e44-79a1-5658-a783-9ae9824ce60b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051752}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c3a7db47-e883-5a71-8bfd-ec843bd98b41" :question/math-academy-id "q-170852" :question/problem "$2$ is prime, **or** $14$ is a multiple of $7$ **and** $5.$\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $R:2\\text{ is prime}$\n\n- $S:14\\text{ is a multiple of }7$\n\n- $T:14\\text{ is a multiple of }5$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $2$ is prime. This corresponds to $R.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $14$ is a multiple of $7$ and $5.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{14\\text{ is a multiple of }7}_{⏟}}_{S}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{14\\text{ is a multiple of }5}_{⏟}}_{T},\n$$\n\nthat is, $S∧T.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{2\\text{ is prime}}_{⏟}}_{R}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{14\\text{ is a multiple of }7\\text{ and }5}_{⏟}}_{S\\,∧\\,T},\n$$\n\nthat is, $R∨(S∧T).$"} :step/id #uuid "8cb69003-9c5b-5348-b98b-bc7093eea6f5" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565537}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565537 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379005 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "398dfebf-2715-5754-8536-2fbf57b13ec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379007} {:answer/id #uuid "6bbd595e-8862-5ddd-ad65-9bbe8a1503d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379008}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379008} :answer-field/id #uuid "a73e4d24-a544-5df8-926d-0dd2efcec4c1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379006} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7724fa1-404c-5cf6-a1e4-ffe8e50a65bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379010} {:answer/id #uuid "f6b3e6af-d78b-5785-9381-3f1554e4df26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379011}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379011} :answer-field/id #uuid "8de5b0f9-3915-5928-8eee-ebfbdd12e385" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379009} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e7d887d-e0e7-5390-878c-560d04e1e11f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379013} {:answer/id #uuid "1f1049a9-d8a0-54f8-b526-d6d1108f314b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379014}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379013} :answer-field/id #uuid "576ab971-a207-5967-8d37-5db8a4c60c7d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379012}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b8a204fe-0678-5217-8fd6-73d54f821b1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-175909" :question/problem "$$\n{{\\sqrt{2}\\text{ is irrational}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{1-2=1}_{⏟}}_{B}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $A$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $B$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $A∨B$ is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $A$ is true, and $B$ is false. Therefore, the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{\\sqrt{2}\\text{ is irrational}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{1-2=1}_{⏟}}_{B} & \\,\\,≡\\,\\text{true}∨\\text{false}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "e564f1c7-8cb6-50b6-a505-2ce605981f41" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565487}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565538 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055087 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f4e9e86-8284-5124-a5d8-2986c678430f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051966} {:answer/id #uuid "351e3b6e-328b-51b3-a3b4-654ed5082185" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051967}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051967} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f130160-11dc-5d3a-9856-5fbf9e017de3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051965} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a784ae67-278a-5990-a46b-9305f5e46ed4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051969} {:answer/id #uuid "ec33348b-a0de-5fdb-82f8-56f288950968" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051970}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051969} :answer-field/id #uuid "80f5e149-319b-5aca-8113-65c296ae9284" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051968} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0974b375-a54a-5d5e-846e-11f8487271d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051972} {:answer/id #uuid "40bf36f3-987d-514b-a937-3a85bd10e5c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051973}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051973} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbf02d32-be98-53f4-bb26-71699b829f9f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051971}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "251d1784-5e7a-5d2b-9609-81be8de6d435" :question/math-academy-id "q-181713" :question/problem "$$\n{{2\\text{ is negative}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{0.5\\text{ is rational}}_{⏟}}_{B}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $A$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $B$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $A∨B$ is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $A$ is false, and $B$ is true. Therefore, the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{2\\text{ is negative}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{0.5\\text{ is rational}}_{⏟}}_{B} & \\,\\,≡\\,\\text{false}∨\\text{true}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "e5df0196-87e7-5d2d-a973-8fd272f8b83b"}] :activity/title "The \"And\" and \"Or\" Connectives" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564930}]}
